---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Intro from "../components/Intro.astro";
import FacebookNews from "../components/FacebookNews.astro";
import SeasonCards from "../components/SeasonCards.astro";
import OfferOverview from "../components/OfferOverview.astro";
import Compositions from "../components/Compositions.astro";
import GalleryShow from "../components/GalleryShow.astro";
import Directions from "../components/Directions.astro";
import { homeGallery } from "../data/gallery";

/**
 * The home page: what is new this week, what the holding sells, which part of the year is
 * running, what it looks like, and how to get there.
 *
 * ## Why the news stands first
 *
 * `FacebookNews` moved from second-to-last to directly under the hero in September 2026, on
 * the owner's instruction. The argument is the one the block was built on: the catalogue
 * changes once a season, and this is the only thing on the page that can differ between two
 * Tuesdays. Someone who was here in May and comes back in October should be told that the
 * chrysanthemums are out before they are told anything they already know.
 *
 * It costs the hero its position as the only thing above the fold, and that was weighed: the
 * `h1`, the tagline and the call button are still the first things in the document and still
 * the first thing read. What follows them is now news rather than the calendar.
 *
 * ## Where the photo show sits, and why there
 *
 * `GalleryShow` went the other way in the same change, from between the offer tiles and the
 * plantings to between the plantings and the map. It is not a preference. The sections
 * alternate light and dark, two dark plates cannot be told apart from each other (--green-band
 * in tokens.css explains why the usable range is that narrow), and the news block used to be
 * the light band between `Compositions` and `Directions`. Taking it to the top left those two
 * plates touching, and the show is the section that can stand between them: it is light, it
 * belongs after the plantings rather than before them - the tiles say what is sold, the
 * plantings say what can be made of it, the show says what all of it looks like - and it
 * leaves the offer tiles next to `--paper-clay`, which is the arrangement the top of this page
 * already uses.
 *
 * So the order of sections on this page is a correctness constraint and not a layout taste.
 * Light, light, dark, light, dark, light, dark:
 *
 *   Intro          --paper
 *   FacebookNews   --paper-clay
 *   SeasonCards    --green-band
 *   OfferOverview  --paper-clay
 *   Compositions   --green-band
 *   GalleryShow    --paper
 *   Directions     --green-band
 *
 * Two light grounds may touch - they differ in hue and the rules do the parting. Two dark ones
 * may not. The last join, --green-band against the --ink footer, is 1.44:1 and is the one that
 * cannot be fixed; the footer colour is not up for negotiation.
 *
 * **The hero's ground is the newest line in that table and it was decided by the join under
 * it.** It stood on --paper-blush, which against the news block's --paper-clay is 1.003:1 - one
 * colour, not two - so the first join on the page read as a stray hairline rather than as a
 * boundary. --paper makes it 1.079:1, the most this palette allows between two light grounds;
 * blush left tokens.css with it, because nothing else stood on it. Three variants were built
 * and looked at side by side before this one was taken, and the two that lost are recorded in
 * docs/inwentaryzacja.md.
 *
 * The show carries **69 photographs** - every frame of the offer that is the holding's own and
 * is not already on this page - one row at a time. That is not 69 photographs' worth of page:
 * `gallery-show.ts` mounts three rows and hides the rest, and a hidden image is never fetched.
 * The "Więcej zdjęć" row under it points at `#zdjecia` on each category page, which is the
 * strip that holds that group's full set.
 *
 * This page used to be the entire site - fourteen plant descriptions, the gallery, the history
 * and the contact section on one scroll, with a menu whose five entries pointed at three
 * anchors. Cutting it back to an intro, the season and four tiles then went too far the other
 * way: the holding has 48 photographs of its own, that entrance showed four of them, and the
 * offer tiles carried none at all - on a business whose whole product is what a plant looks
 * like.
 *
 * **So this page shows the pictures, and only the pictures.** It is a preview of each part of
 * the site rather than a table of contents for it - but a preview, not a copy. The subpages
 * keep what makes them worth opening: the cultivation descriptions, the filters, the phone
 * numbers.
 *
 * Outline: `h1` in Intro, then one `h2` per section.
 *
 * ## The two blocks that repeat something, and what earns them their place
 *
 * - **Inspiracje** shows the same 23 plantings as `/inspiracje/`, with the filter, the
 *   thumbnail rail, the anchors, the structured data and the per-panel phone CTA all switched
 *   off (see the props on `Compositions.astro`). Every panel heading is a link to that planting
 *   on `/inspiracje/`, so the preview feeds the page rather than replacing it.
 * - **Directions** stands where `ContactStrip` stood in 0.5, and would deserve the same
 *   deletion if it repeated what that one did. It does not: it prints no phone number. The
 *   strip was removed because the same number appeared three times on this page - in the Intro
 *   call button, in the strip and in the footer. The block answers the one question the footer
 *   cannot: where this is, on a map.
 *
 * **The phone count is the thing to watch on this page, and it is easy to get wrong.** The
 * first draft of 0.7 shipped the plantings strip with its panel CTA intact and put the number
 * on this page **25 times** - once in the Intro, once in the footer and once in each of the 23
 * panels - while this very comment claimed it appeared once. Anything repeated per panel is
 * repeated 23 times here. Count it on the built page before trusting a sentence about it:
 * `grep -o 'href="tel:' dist/index.html | wc -l` should read **3**: the intro's one CTA plus
 * the footer's list of both numbers. The check used to name a number - `602 518 401` - which
 * stopped existing when the owners withdrew two of the four phones, so it was passing by
 * matching nothing. Count the links, not a particular number.
 *
 * ## The block that is not a preview of anything
 *
 * **Aktualności** (`FacebookNews`) is the one thing on this page with no subpage behind it.
 * The catalogue changes once a season; this is where "chryzantemy są już w sprzedaży" can
 * appear on a Tuesday, because the owners write it on Facebook and a workflow carries it here.
 *
 * It renders whether or not there are posts. Until September 2026 that was load-bearing - it
 * was the light band between two dark plates - and it no longer is, because the block does not
 * stand between two dark plates any more. The empty state stays all the same, on the owners'
 * own decision: a block that is always there, saying where the news lives, rather than a
 * section that comes and goes with a token.
 *
 * The map is consent-gated, and the Facebook block needs no gate because it embeds nothing -
 * its pictures and its films are our own files. So the home page still contacts nothing but
 * our own server until a visitor asks for the map.
 */

const galleryGroups = await homeGallery();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Kwiaty balkonowe i chryzantemy - „Saran”, Kazimierz Dolny"
  description="Kwiaty balkonowe, rabatowe i chryzantemy wielkokwiatowe z własnej uprawy. Rodzinne gospodarstwo w Cholewiance pod Kazimierzem Dolnym. Zamówienia telefonicznie."
  canonical="/"
>
  <Intro />
  <FacebookNews />
  <SeasonCards />
  <OfferOverview />
  <Compositions
    level={2}
    showFilters={false}
    showRail={false}
    structuredData={false}
    ids={false}
    prose={false}
    allLink
    ground="dark"
  />
  <GalleryShow groups={galleryGroups} />
  <Directions />
</BaseLayout>
